## 11. Frontend — SIP.js Hook (useSoftphone.ts — 338 lines)

| Feature | Implementation | Lines |
|---|---|---|
| **UserAgent creation** | WSS transport + ICE servers + auth password | 97-111 |
| **Registerer** | `register()` on start, `unregister()` on cleanup | 113-153 |
| **Inbound handling** | `ua.delegate.onInvite` → ring state, NOT auto-accept | 123-146 |
| **Ringtone** | `AudioContext` oscillator (440Hz sine, on/off pattern) | 15-53 |
| **Ringtone start** | On inbound `onInvite` | 133 |
| **Ringtone stop** | On accept (163), reject (197), remote cancel (142) | ✅ All 3 paths |
| **acceptIncoming()** | `invitation.accept()` + media attach + store update | 157-188 |
| **rejectIncoming()** | `invitation.reject()` + clear state | 191-198 |
| **call()** (outbound) | `new Inviter()` + state listener + `inviter.invite()` | 201-244 |
| **hangup()** | `bye()` if established, `cancel()` if establishing | 247-258 |
| **mute()** | Toggle `sender.track.enabled` on audio senders | 261-274 |
| **hold()** | Toggle senders AND receivers `track.enabled` | 277-297 |
| **sendDtmf()** | SIP INFO with `application/dtmf-relay` body | 299-318 |
| **attachRemoteMedia()** | Gets receivers → MediaStream → `<audio>` element | 323-337 |

**Verdict: ✅ 100% — Full SIP lifecycle + DTMF + ringtone**

